Ukraine's major attack on Russia's Ust-Luga port last week succeeded thanks to an impressive command-and-control system, Estonian Defense Forces Lt. Col. Marten Suur told ERR.
Although the exact number of drones sent toward the Ust-Luga area is unknown, it was likely around 1,000, Suur said. The drones were reportedly gathered near the target area and held in a loitering pattern until a sufficient number had assembled.
